{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>As you saw</b> — the reason they mix is that all of them take gentile daughters, as the Persians take the Babylonian women, and the Arabians [Shebans] take the Egyptian women, and these are not like those in their form and in their clothing and their food and their custom, also disagreement in their law, and even the sons of Ham who are toward the southwest across the sea and they are adjacent to the Great Sea, which is called Oceanus."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:22.511473002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}